 length "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"wordLength"},{"type":"text","text":" over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"alphabetSize"},{"type":"text","text":" letters, and an arc from each word to the m words its last n − 1 letters"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"begin. Word a₁…aₙ is vertex Σ aᵢ·m^(n−i), so its successors are (u·m mod mⁿ) + a."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"mⁿ vertices, mⁿ⁺¹ arcs, in row-major order; each constant word has a self-loop, so the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph is built on the representations that allow them. Every vertex has in- and out-degree"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"m. O(mⁿ⁺¹) expected."}],"url":"\/documentation\/namedgraphs\/adjacencylistmodule\/adjacencylist\/debruijn(alphabetsize:wordlength:)","kind":"symbol","title":"deBruijn(alphabetSize:wordLength:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/NamedGraphs\/documentation\/NamedGraphs\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/deBruijn(alphabetSize:wordLength:)"},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent":{"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent","abstract":[{"text":"A generic, high-performance graph library for Swift.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/grafluent","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"Grafluent"},"doc://AdjacencyListModule/documentation/AdjacencyListModule/AdjacencyList":{"title":"AdjacencyList","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AdjacencyList","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AdjacencyList","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/adjacencylistmodule\/adjacencylist","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed graph stored as out- and in-adjacency lists."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluen